### 1. Mathematical Foundations & Memory Architecture

#### Memory Tagging & Invariants
- Let pointer $P \in \mathbb{N}$ represent an 8-byte aligned heap address where the least significant bit (LSB) indicates logical deletion:
  $$\text{Mark}(P) = P \mid 0\text{x}1, \quad \text{Unmark}(P) = P \ \& \ \sim 0\text{x}1, \quad \text{IsMarked}(P) = (P \ \& \ 0\text{x}1) \ne 0$$
- **Tower Invariant**: For any index node $N$, if level $k$ is marked for deletion, all levels $j > k$ must already be marked. Physical unlinking progresses top-down ($L-1 \to 0$) or bottom-up via helping.
- **MVCC Visibility Invariant**: For a read snapshot $T_{\text{read}}$, a version $V$ is visible iff:
  $$\text{created\_tx\_id}(V) \le T_{\text{read}} < \text{deleted\_tx\_id}(V)$$
  where $\text{deleted\_tx\_id} = \infty$ represents an active, un-overwritten record.

