### Low-Level Synchronization & Memory Ordering Invariants

| Component | Operation | Memory Ordering | Invariant & Correctness Guarantee |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`MvccIndex`** | `buckets[i].load()` | `Acquire` | Synchronizes with `cas_head` `Release`. Guarantees readers observe all payload bytes and previous `next` links without observing partial state or stale pointers. |
| **`MvccIndex`** | `buckets[i].cas()` | `AcqRel` | **Acquire** loads the freshest head record during CAS retries. **Release** publishes the newly allocated `VersionRecord` pointer to concurrent readers. |
| **`VersionRecord`** | `tx_id_deleted.store()` | `Release` | Superseding an existing head version stores `commit_tx_id`. Readers inspecting `tx_id_deleted` with `Acquire` are guaranteed to see the retirement timestamp. |
| **`VersionRecord`** | `next.load()` | `Acquire` | Wait-free traversal down the historical chain. Ensures each preceding historical version's memory layout is visible. |
| **`EpochManager`** | `slots[i].local_epoch` | `Release` / `SeqCst` Fence | Announces entry into critical section. The subsequent `SeqCst` fence ensures thread-local epoch publication happens-before the traversal of `MvccIndex` nodes. |
| **`WalAppender`** | `buf_offset.store()` | `Release` | Direct write batch boundary update. Ensures all raw frame bytes copied to the 4KB-aligned arena are visible before updating the flush cursor. |

