### 2. Formal Memory Order Proof & Barrier Rationale

```
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                               CRITICAL ATOMIC OPERATIONS & BARRIERS                                |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| Atomic Operation                   | Memory Ordering          | Formal Synchronization Rationale   |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| write_head_.compare_exchange_weak  | success: acq_rel         | Acquire establishes visibility of  |
|                                    | failure: relaxed         | prior reservations. Release ensures|
|                                    |                          | monotonic allocation order.        |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| read_tail_.load (producer check)   | acquire                  | Synchronizes-with consumer release |
|                                    |                          | & slot reset to STATUS_EMPTY before|
|                                    |                          | overwriting ring buffer memory.    |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| MsgHeader::state.store             | release                  | Synchronizes-with cascade_commit   |
| (STATUS_COMMITTED/STATUS_SKIPPED)  |                          | & reader load. Guarantees non-     |
|                                    |                          | atomic payload writes are visible. |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| write_commit_.compare_exchange_weak| success: acq_rel         | Acquire loads next frame state;    |
| (cascade_commit)                   | failure: acquire         | Release publishes continuous batch |
|                                    |                          | to downstream consumers.           |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| read_head_.compare_exchange_weak   | success: acq_rel         | Acquire sees committed data writes;|
| (acquire_read_lease)               | failure: acquire         | Release reserves distinct slice    |
|                                    |                          | preventing duplicate reader access.|
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| MsgHeader::state.store             | release                  | Ensures payload read finishes      |
| (STATUS_RELEASED)                  |                          | before slot is marked reclaimable. |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
| read_tail_.compare_exchange_weak   | success: acq_rel         | AcqRel synchronizes reset state with|
| (cascade_tail)                     | failure: acquire         | producers, safely freeing capacity.|
+------------------------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------------+
```

#### Happens-Before & Synchronizes-With Graph

$$\begin{aligned}
\text{Producer } P_i: & \quad \text{Write payload non-atomically} \xrightarrow{\text{sequenced-before}} \text{store}(\text{COMMITTED}, \texttt{release}) \\
& \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \quad \downarrow \text{\textit{synchronizes-with}} \\
\text{Committer / Consumer}: & \quad \text{load}(\text{COMMITTED}, \texttt{acquire}) \xrightarrow{\text{happens-before}} \text{Read payload non-atomically}
\end{aligned}$$

1. **Non-Atomic Payload Safety:** Producers write variable-length payloads directly into the circular buffer with plain stores. The producer then executes `MsgHeader::state.store(STATUS_COMMITTED, std::memory_order_release)`. Any reader or cascading commit thread observing this status via `state.load(std::memory_order_acquire)` establishes a formal *synchronizes-with* relationship, guaranteeing that all byte stores to the payload *happen-before* the consumer reads them.
2. **ABA & Wrap-Around Elimination:** Each frame header embeds an 8-bit `epoch` computed as `(pos / Capacity) & 0xFF`. A slot is only recognized as valid if `hdr_epoch == expected_epoch`. Stale reads from previous buffer revolutions are deterministically rejected.
3. **Cacheline Bouncing Elimination:** The 4 hot cursors (`write_head_`, `write_commit_`, `read_head_`, `read_tail_`) are isolated onto independent 64-byte/128-byte cache lines using `alignas(hardware_destructive_interference_size)`. Producer-local (`tl_cached_tail`) and consumer-local (`tl_cached_commit`) thread-local views eliminate inter-core coherence invalidations on the fast path.

