### 1. Mathematical & Formal Specification

#### System Model & Definitions
Let the priority queue $\mathcal{Q}$ manage elements $e = (p, v)$, where $p \in \{0, 1, \dots, P-1\}$ denotes the priority level ($0$ being the highest priority) and $v \in T$ is the payload. The structure is partitioned into $P$ priority bands, each comprising $K$ distinct lock-free lanes $\mathcal{L}_{p, 0}, \dots, \mathcal{L}_{p, K-1}$.

```
                 Priority Level 0 (Highest)
                 +-----------+-----------+-----+-------------+
                 |  Lane 0   |  Lane 1   | ... |  Lane K-1   |
                 +-----------+-----------+-----+-------------+
                                       ...
                 Priority Level P-1 (Lowest)
                 +-----------+-----------+-----+-------------+
                 |  Lane 0   |  Lane 1   | ... |  Lane K-1   |
                 +-----------+-----------+-----+-------------+
```

---

#### Formal Invariants & Staleness Bounds

1. **Cell State Invariant:**  
   Each lane $\mathcal{L}_{p, k}$ is implemented as a circular buffer with monotonically increasing cell sequence numbers $S[i]$. A cell at index $i$ is writable for cycle $c$ if and only if $S[i] = 2c$, and readable if and only if $S[i] = 2c + 1$.
2. **$\epsilon$-Staleness Bound:**  
   Let $p_{\min}(t)$ be the global minimum priority level containing at least one unconsumed element at time $t$. An extraction operation $op_{\text{pop}}$ returning an element with priority $p_{\text{ret}}$ satisfies:
   $$p_{\text{ret}} \le p_{\min}(t) + \epsilon$$
   where $\epsilon \in \mathbb{N}_0$ is the relaxation bound determined by the power-of-two lane sampling window. When power-of-two sampling probes $d \ge 2$ independent lanes within the active band, the probability of selecting an element older than the top-$m$ elements decays exponentially:
   $$\mathbb{P}(\text{staleness} > k) \le \left(1 - \frac{k}{K}\right)^d$$

---

#### Linearization Points

| Operation | Condition | Linearization Point (LP) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `push(p, v)` | **Success** | The atomic `fetch_add` or successful CAS on the cell's sequence number $S[i]$ in lane $\mathcal{L}_{p, k}$ transitioning the cell from state $2c \to 2c+1$ with `std::memory_order_release`. |
| `push(p, v)` | **Lane Full** | The atomic load of the lane tail/head sequence showing $\text{tail} - \text{head} \ge \text{Capacity}$ with `std::memory_order_acquire`. |
| `pop_min()` | **Success** | The atomic CAS on the cell's sequence number $S[i]$ in lane $\mathcal{L}_{p, k}$ transitioning the cell from $2c+1 \to 2(c+1)$ with `std::memory_order_acq_rel`. |
| `pop_min()` | **Empty** | Atomic linearization read across all priority band summary bitmasks witnessing $\text{Bitmask} = 0$ via `std::memory_order_acquire`. |

---

#### Progress & Memory Safety Guarantees

* **Lock-Freedom of Push/Pop:** Every lane operation is bounded by atomic sequence increments and CAS operations. Even if $M-1$ threads are suspended arbitrarily at any instruction, at least one active thread will successfully advance its cell sequence in finite steps, satisfying lock-freedom.
* **Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR) Safety:** An object retired at global epoch $e$ is only physically freed when all active threads have registered an observed epoch $e_t \ge e + 1$. Because no thread in epoch $\ge e + 1$ can acquire a pointer to an object unlinked in epoch $e$, use-after-free and ABA hazards are strictly eliminated.
* **Non-Blocking Thread Termination:** Retiring threads flush local retired lists to a lock-free orphan list, ensuring zero leaks upon thread exit without blocking concurrent active mutators.

