### 4. Failure Analysis & Trade-off Matrix

| Edge Case / Failure Vector | System State & Architectural Behavior | Mitigation / Resolution Strategy | Latency & Performance Impact |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **OS Thread Preemption inside `append()`** | Producer reserves an LSN via atomic `fetch_add` but context-switches before updating the slot sequence to `READY_FOR_FLUSH`. | Flusher reactor runs a bounded speculative pause loop (`_mm_pause()`). If deadline expires, lease tombstone is stamped, leapfrogging the stalled slot. The stalled producer resumes, detects the tombstone, and re-claims a new LSN. | Zero impact on other concurrent writers; bounded $P_{99.9}$ flusher jitter ($< 50\ \mu s$). |
| **Ring Buffer Sched Backpressure (Queue Full)** | Writers ingest records faster than NVMe commit latency ($> 1.5\text{M}$ ops/sec saturation), causing slot sequence to lag behind claim counter. | Writers loop on `slot.sequence.load(acquire)` and invoke `_mm_pause()` instructions. Eliminates dynamic allocation and cache-line invalidation. | Latency shifts from wait-free ingestion to bounded spin-wait directly reflecting underlying device Direct I/O throughput limits. |
