# 4. Failure Analysis & Edge Case Trade-off Matrix

| Failure Mode / Edge Case | Failure Mechanics | Resolution Mechanism in WAL Engine | Trade-off / Architectural Invariant |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Stalled / Preempted Producer** | A writer thread obtains an LSN ticket via `fetch_add`, but is preempted by the kernel scheduler before publishing to the slot. | **Speculative Skip Lease:** Flusher scans with bounded spin/timestamp ($50\ \mu s$). If timeout expires, flusher executes a CAS transition to `SLOT_SKIPPED`, writes a NOP frame, and advances. | Sacrifices a few bytes of WAL disk space to preserve global ingestion latency and eliminate pipeline deadlocks. |
| **Ring Buffer Saturated (Backpressure)** | Ingestion rate exceeds NVMe write bandwidth ($> 1.5\text{M ops/sec}$ burst), filling the 64MB buffer before kernel flush. | **Tight Backpressure Barrier:** Producer checks distance between `sequence_tail_` and `flushed_offset_`. If $\ge \text{RING\_BUFFER\_SIZE}$, producer executes `_mm_pause()` spins. | Prevents buffer overrun without dynamic heap allocation. Introduces latency degradation on writers under sustained overload. |
| **Kernel Submission Queue (`SQ`) Saturated** | High concurrent bursts exhaust `io_uring` submission queue entries (`SQE`). | **Synchronous Flush Drain:** When `io_uring_get_sqe` yields `nullptr`, flusher immediately calls `io_uring_submit` and drains pending completions before retrying. | Bounds kernel tracking memory overhead while maintaining sub-microsecond batch processing. |
| **Torn Page at Sector Boundary** | Power loss occurs mid-write of a 4096-byte sector, leaving half-written data on the disk. | **Strict Framing Verification:** Recovery scans magic bytes, sizes, and hardware CRC32C. The first corrupted CRC or non-matching magic terminates recovery at that sector boundary. | Guarantees zero corrupted or uncommitted transactions enter state-machine replay; uncommitted tail is cleanly truncated. |
| **Out-of-Order Direct I/O Completion** | Kernel writes multiple asynchronous blocks non-contiguously. | **Monotonic Barrier Watermarking:** Fixed buffer ordering guarantees disk writes follow ring index ordering. Watermark LSN updates only advance upon receiving confirmed CQE records. | Guarantees strict causal ordering ($A \to B \implies \text{LSN}_A < \text{LSN}_B$) across concurrent caller threads. |

