### 4. Failure Analysis & Edge-Case Engineering Matrix

| Failure Mode / Edge Case | System Impact | Detection Mechanism | Resolution & Mitigation Architecture |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Stalled / Preempted Writer Thread** | Producer claims LSN via `fetch_add` but gets preempted while writing payload; flusher drain hits a non-`READY` slot. | Flusher loop detects a slot with status `WRITING` or `CLAIMED` while scanning ahead of `local_flush_head`. | **Bounded Speculative Scan:** The flusher yields for a small threshold (e.g., $50\ \mu\text{s}$). If the stall exceeds the lease timeout, the engine writes a speculative `TOMBSTONE` padding record across the uncommitted range, advances the durable head, and forces the stalled producer to fail/retry with a new LSN upon wake-up. |
| **Ring Saturation & Backpressure** | Producer write rate outpaces disk throughput ($R_{\text{ingest}} > R_{\text{disk}}$), threatening to overwrite un-flushed slots. | Slot reservation condition checks `assigned_lsn - durable_lsn > capacity`. | **Wait-Free Yield & Exponential Backoff:** Writers poll `durable_lsn.load(relaxed)` and execute cooperative pause/yield operations without locking, preventing ring corruption. |
| **Kernel `io_uring` Submission Queue (SQ) Overflow** | Writer batching generates SQEs faster than the kernel consumes them. | `io_uring_get_sqe()` returns `nullptr`. | **Automatic Sync Drain:** Immediately triggers synchronous kernel flush via `io_uring_submit(&ring_)` and loops until an SQE slot opens up. CQ size is overprovisioned $2\times$ SQ size to avoid CQ drops. |
| **Torn Page Writes on Power Outage** | 4KB sector is partially written or unaligned Direct-I/O flush is interrupted mid-flight during power loss. | `CrashRecoveryEngine` detects CRC32C failure or incomplete header frame in the last direct I/O block. | **Truncate-to-HWM:** Scans verify header CRC + payload CRC independently. On mismatch, recovery safely truncates the segment at the last valid LSN high-water mark ($HWM$), discarding incomplete torn sectors. |
| **Weak Memory Model Store Reordering** | ARM64 / PowerPC CPUs reorder payload writes after slot status publication, exposing corrupted data to the flusher. | Thread Sanitizer (TSan) or data CRC corruption under concurrency on aarch64. | **Strict Release-Acquire Barriers:** Producer transitions status to `READY_FOR_FLUSH` using `std::memory_order_release`. Flusher inspects status with `std::memory_order_acquire`, guaranteeing memory visibility across all architectures. |

