### Formal Explanation of the Memory Model & Ordering Proof

| Operation / Path | Atomic Primitive & Ordering | Formal Invariant / Race-Free Guarantee |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **MPSC Tail Append (Commit Queue)** | `tail.compare_exchange_weak(..., Ordering::Release, Ordering::Relaxed)` | Guarantees that the follower’s `CommitRequest` (with payload & LSN initialized) is fully visible before any thread traverses or links it to the tail. |
| **Leader Handoff & Election** | `leader_lock.compare_exchange(false, true, Ordering::Acquire, Ordering::Relaxed)` / `store(false, Ordering::Release)` | Creates an acquire-release synchronization edge between successive batch leaders. Prevents concurrent DMA buffer writes and ensures prior batch DMA operations complete before the next leader starts assembling a batch. |
| **Batch Completion Notification** | `req.completed.store(1, Ordering::Release)` $\rightarrow$ `req.completed.load(Ordering::Acquire)` | Guarantees that all disk writes and datasync completions across `io_uring` are committed to non-volatile storage before followers wake up and observe status `1`. |
| **MVCC Version Chain Insertion** | `head.compare_exchange_weak(..., Ordering::Release, Ordering::Relaxed)` | Ensures the newly allocated `VersionNode` fields (`lsn`, `val`, `prev`) are globally visible before other reader threads can observe the new node at `head`. |
| **RCU Wait-Free Traversals** | `head.load(Ordering::Acquire)` $\rightarrow$ `node.prev.load(Ordering::Acquire)` | Ensures readers observe consistent initialized node payloads without holding locks. Combined with `EpochGuard::pin(SeqCst)`, readers never access freed memory because epochs cannot advance past active pins. |
| **EBR Epoch Transitions** | `global_epoch.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Release)` + 3-epoch rotation | Guarantees an unlinked `VersionNode` in slot $E$ is only reclaimed when all threads have advanced beyond epoch $E+1$. Zero double-free or use-after-free anomalies can occur. |
